  off-device, so this ships ONE look at a time for you to judge on screen and steer.
  • STEP 1 — RINGS look: was a soft sinusoidal wash (0.5+0.5·sin) → read as a blurry rainbow
    haze, which also broke our own "no soft gradients/glow" rule. Now it's a PHYSICALLY correct
    interference field: two radial wave trains are superposed and the visible value is their
    INTENSITY = amplitude² (energy ∝ amplitude²) → crisp bright fringes on a dark field, like
    real wave interference. Coherence does the physical double-duty: it both detunes the second
    train (high coherence = wide ordered fringes, low = turbulent moiré) AND sharpens the
    maxima (coherent light → thin crisp rings; incoherent → washed). Colour unchanged this step.
